<http://data.silknow.org/object/2e291e87-2dea-31d6-92ab-12c14ab06331>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "A pair of kid gloves with blue silk ribbon applied on gauntlet and covered with dense embroidery in silver and silver-gilt thread, strip and purl."@en , "This leather glove demonstrates the lavish style of metal embroidery popular in the 1660s. The whole gauntlet is encrusted with densely worked silver and silver-gilt purl (tiny coils of very fine metal wire) and strip. An edging of blue grosgrain ribbon underneath the embroidery can only just be seen. Gloves were a popular choice of gift in the 17th century. It was customary to present the monarch with a pair at New Year, and gloves were also frequently exchanged as wedding gifts."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/0ad327df-146f-3c73-9a29-afda0ad81a4f> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/e08fffc2-2c35-38e9-95b8-18f48f2e601e> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/e416f207-13b2-31aa-a60e-1766c563ae2c> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/cfc6c839-f75d-3e07-90be-a896eb4eaeee> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/7e08eaae-c844-32ed-865e-280cac90cd95> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "This leather glove demonstrates the lavish style of metal embroidery popular in the 1660s. The whole gauntlet is encrusted with densely worked silver and silver-gilt purl (tiny coils of very fine metal wire) and strip. An edging of blue grosgrain ribbon underneath the embroidery can only just be seen. Gloves were a popular choice of gift in the 17th century. It was customary to present the monarch with a pair at New Year, and gloves were also frequently exchanged as wedding gifts."@en , "A pair of kid gloves with blue silk ribbon applied on gauntlet and covered with dense embroidery in silver and silver-gilt thread, strip and purl."@en ;
        dc:identifier                  "T.202&A-1928" ;
